 "grid_note": "HOW THE CELLS WERE LOCATED, because a mark one column off is a person of the wrong age and the method has to be inspectable. The 39 vertical rules were fitted as a single pitch off the empty right-hand columns of the same image and the fit was CHECKED AGAINST THE PRINTED HEADING — column 1 must be 'Under 5', column 27 'Under 10' under FREE COLORED MALES — before any cell was read. The 31 ruled lines were fitted the same way and checked against the names. Every cell was then cut out at that grid, and the ones carrying ink were read one at a time as images; a cell the eye rejected as paper grain or a ruled line is recorded as empty. No cell value here is an OCR output.",
 "cells_state": "partial",
 "cells_note": "THE CELLS WERE READ AND ARE MOSTLY NOT COMMITTED, which is the rule this ticket was given: a column is committed only where the lines this pass read SUM to the figure the enumerator wrote at the foot of the sheet, and every column that does not is left unreconciled with its residual stated rather than forced. `cells` carries only the balanced columns. `cells_first_pass` carries the whole reading, balanced or not, so the next reader starts from a reading rather than from the sheet — it is NOT reconciled data and nothing downstream may treat it as such.",
